# NOTE: this file is written and must be read via nitransforms
# (nitransforms.linear.load(path, fmt='fs').matrix), not FreeSurfer's own LTA
# tools -- nitransforms stores LTAs using FreeSurfer's "points convention",
# so the raw matrix numbers above are NOT the intended physical transform
# directly; only round-tripping through nitransforms' reader/writer gives
# back the correct matrix.
# Maps the raw EBB-MRI scan's (0.5mm_EBB-MRI.nii.gz) own native RAS to true
# MNI RAS. Equal to the plain inverse of reg_EBBMRI_to_MNI/affine.lta's matrix
# -- NOT squared. Verified empirically: reg_EBBMRI_to_MNI/0.5mm_EBB-MRI.moved.nii.gz's
# own vox2ras equals inv(affine.lta) @ (0.5mm_EBB-MRI.nii.gz's vox2ras) to
# float32 precision (~1e-5 max abs diff on the full matrix). An earlier
# version of this file assumed affine.lta needed squaring (since
# nitorch_register_EBB-MRI_to_MNI.sh runs "@affine affine -g", a symmetric
# registration) -- that assumption was wrong; empirically only a single
# inversion is needed to reproduce the real moved.nii.gz header exactly.
